# 53. BUSINESS OWNER AUTHORIZATION

This rule is mandatory:

A business owner can only modify businesses that belong to that owner.

Never implement:

```python
business = get_business(id)
business.update(...)
```

without verifying ownership.

Correct concept:

```text
authenticated owner
        ↓
business ownership check
        ↓
authorized modification
```

---

# 54. ADMIN AUTHORIZATION

Do not simply check:

```text
is_logged_in == true
```

for admin endpoints.

Require:

```text
role == ADMIN
```

and later support more granular permissions if necessary.

