---

# 90. ADMIN FRONTEND

Protect all admin routes.

If a normal student navigates directly to:

```text
/admin
```

they must not receive administrative data.

Authorization must also be enforced by the backend.

Frontend protection is only UX.

Backend authorization is security.

---

# 91. BUSINESS OWNER FRONTEND

Same principle.

Do not trust:

```text
business_id
```

coming from the client.

Backend must determine whether the authenticated owner controls that business.

---

# 92. REVIEW AUTHORIZATION

A student can edit/delete only their own review, subject to product policy.

An owner can only respond to reviews belonging to their business.

An admin can moderate according to permission.

---

# 93. IMAGE MODERATION FUTURE

